            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0410" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-27T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received May 27—6:05
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>593. Legation’s 580, May 23, 3 p.m.; and 588, May 25, 4 p.m. Lockhart reports
                    that, Standard Oil Company having approved, their vessels <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mei Foo</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Mei Chuen</hi>
                    left for Ichang morning 26th escorted by U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pigeon</hi> to evacuate oil stocks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
